@4417   = ~Fools! Phaere has died, and all our lives are now forfeit as well.~
@4418   = ~No! Please... don't!~
@4419   = ~Slaver~
@4420   = ~Slaver~
@4421   = ~This blade burns with a magical fire, and a charring blast is released whenever a hit is scored. "Meta Infernum" is etched on the hilt, though it appears somewhat faded and may not be original to the sword.

STATISTICS:

THAC0: +1
Damage: 1d8+1, +1 fire damage
Damage Type: Slashing
Speed Factor: 4
Proficiency Type: Longsword
Type: One-handed
Requires:
 6 Strength

Weight: 4

Not usable by:
 Beast Master
 Cleric
 Druid
 Mage
 Sorcerer~
@4422   = ~Sword of Flame +1~
@4423   = ~Eliya~
@4424   = ~Welcome to this place. I've looked forward to seeing you. I am, as you know, Aran Linvail.~ [ARAN02]
@4425   = ~My thanks, Aran. What would you have of me?~
@4426   = ~~
@4427   = ~Strangely, the magic rolls off of Jon... causing him some mild discomfort but no lasting effects.~
@4428   = ~Right to the point, eh? That's fine with me. You are a very capable person, and I wish to propose a trade of services.~ [ARAN07]
@4429   = ~I propose that you give me what I have coming already. I have paid.~
@4430   = ~It sounds good, though I must see to Imoen. What do you propose as a deal?~
@4431   = ~Dart +5~
@4432   = ~This is your familiar, a dust mephit currently safe within your backpack. The dust mephit is not strong in combat, but it is slightly resistant to magical attack and has the ability to cast the spell Glass Dust twice per day to assist its master.

STATISTICS:

Hit Points: 24
Armor Class: 6
Magic Resistance: 10%

Combat: 2 attacks per round at 13 THAC0 for 1d2 damage
Special abilities:
– 100% resistance to fire
– 50% resistance to slashing, piercing, and missile damage
– Can cast Glitterdust once per day and Glass Dust twice per day (all enemies in a 15-ft. radius must save vs. breath or have their AC penalized by 4 and their THAC0 by 2 for 30 seconds)
– Regenerates 1 HP/round.
– Immune to level drain, sleep, and petrification.

Weight: 1~
@4433   = ~This is your familiar, a fairy dragon, currently curled up and safe within your backpack. The mischievous fairy dragon is fairly resistant to magic... and has the ability to both protect and obscure itself with illusionary magic of its own.

STATISTICS:

Hit Points: 24
Armor Class: 4
Magic Resistance: 32%

Combat: 2 attacks per round at 13 THAC0 for 1d2 damage
Special abilities:
– Can cast Mirror Image and Invisibility, 10' Radius once per day
– Immune to level drain, sleep, and petrification

Weight: 1~
@4434   = ~This is your familiar, a ferret, currently curled up and safe in your backpack. The ferret is an incredibly quick and agile animal, hard to hit and magically made resistant to both damage and spells. The ferret's uncanny ability to get into almost anything unseen makes it a handy pickpocket.

STATISTICS:

Hit Points: 24
Armor Class: 0
Magic Resistance: 50%

Combat: 2 attacks per round at 13 THAC0 for 1d3 damage
Special abilities:
– 75% Pick Pockets
– 40% Hide in Shadows/Move Silently
– 20% Detect Traps
– Can cast Blur once per day
– Immune to level drain, sleep, and petrification

Weight: 1~
@4435   = ~This is your familiar, an imp, currently grumpy yet safe within your backpack. The imp is an unusual creature that is fairly quick and quite resistant to magical spells... and has the ability to cast its own spells on behalf of its master.

STATISTICS:

Hit Points: 18
Armor Class: 2
Magic Resistance: 25%

Combat: 1 attack per round at 15 THAC0 for 1d6 damage
Special abilities:
– 100% resistance to fire, cold, and electricity
– Can cast Polymorph Self once per day
– Regenerates 1 HP/round

Weight: 1~
@4436   = ~This is your familiar, a quasit, currently grumpy yet safe within your backpack. The quasit is a small, infernal creature that is fairly quick and quite resistant to magical spells... and has the ability to cast its own spells on behalf of its master.

STATISTICS:

Hit Points: 24
Armor Class: 2
Magic Resistance: 25%

Combat: 3 attacks per round at 13 THAC0 for 1d6 damage
Special abilities:
– 100% resistance to fire, cold, and electricity
– Can cast Horror and Blur once per day
– Regenerates 1 HP/round

Weight: 1~
@4437   = ~This is your familiar, a pseudo-dragon, currently curled up and safe within your backpack. The lizard-like creature is quite intelligent and fairly well-armored and quick... It does not do much damage in combat, but its magical claws are able to render some enemies unconscious. It is also quite resistant to magical spells.

STATISTICS:

Hit Points: 24
Armor Class: -2
Magic Resistance: 50%

Combat: 2 attacks per round at 13 THAC0 for 1d3 damage, save vs. death or be rendered unconscious for 2 turns
Special abilities:
– Can cast Blur once per day
– Regenerates 1 HP/round
– Immune to level drain, sleep, and petrification

Weight: 1~
@4438   = ~This is your familiar, a rabbit, currently curled up and safe within your backpack. The rabbit might not be one's first choice for a familiar, but this creature is incredibly quick and difficult to hit in combat. The rabbit also has a keen nose for sniffing out traps on behalf of its master.

STATISTICS:

Hit Points: 24
Armor Class: 1
Magic Resistance: 65%

Combat: 2 attacks per round at 13 THAC0 for 1d2 damage
Special abilities:
– 50% Detect Traps
– 30% Hide in Shadows/Move Silently
– 75% resistance to fire, cold, and electricity

Weight: 1~
@4439   = ~Run, child! Get out of here!~ [GORIN02]
@4440   = ~Wait! There is something wrong. We are in an ambush. Prepare yourself!~ [GORIN03]
@4441   = ~You must learn to be patient, child.~ [GORIN04]
@4442   = ~I am a man of peace. Leave us be.~ [GORIN15]
@4443   = ~*cough* *cough* I'm too old for this.~ [GORIN06]
@4444   = ~We have very little time!~ [GORIN07]
@4445   = ~Listen carefully! If we ever become separated, it is imperative that you make your way to the Friendly Arm Inn. There you will meet Khalid and Jaheira. They have long been my friends, and you can trust them.~ [GORIN10]
@4446   = ~Let's hurry, child! The night can only get worse, so we must find shelter soon. Don't worry... I will explain everything as soon as there is time.~ [GORIN11]
@4447   = ~You're a fool if you believe I would trust your benevolence. Step aside and you and your lackeys will be unhurt.~ [GORIN12]
@4448   = ~Awake, my adopted child. Awake, and face the terrible tests ahead of thee.~ [GORIN13]
@4449   = ~I am Death come for thee. Surrender, and thy passage shall be... quicker.~ [NIMBL01]
@4450   = ~So be it, then. Another day you'll die!~ [NIMBL02]
@4451   = ~Hush, little baby, don't say a word. Nimbul's gonna show you the big... black... bird.~ [NIMBL04]
@4452   = ~Taking reward for this easy a kill is almost a crime. Hee hee.~ [NIMBL05]
@4453   = ~Why Nimbul has been hired to deal with the likes of you, I'll never know.~ [NIMBL06]
@4454   = ~Struggle if you must, dead one. I do not mind working for my money.~ [NIMBL07]
@4455   = ~What?! How'd you get in here?~ [MULAH01]
@4456   = ~I yield, I yield to thee!~ [MULAH02]
@4457   = ~Fools, you would turn your back on a servant of Cyric?~ [MULAH03]
@4458   = ~You'll not have me! You'll not, you'll not!~ [MULAH06]
@4459   = ~Help, my minions, help!~ [MULAH07]
@4460   = ~Shhh. I must talk to you in private. These are troubled times.~ [TAMOK01]
@4461   = ~Stupid cretins.~ [TAMOK03]
@4462   = ~Loyalty to one's lord is all that can be expected.~ [TAMOK04]
@4463   = ~In these times, only the strong survive.~ [TAMOK05]
@4464   = ~A secret is only a secret if kept to oneself.~ [TAMOK06]
@4465   = ~I have nothing else to say.~ [TAMOK07]
@4466   = ~Watch your words! I'm in a foul mood!~ [TAZOK01]
@4467   = ~The longer the fight, the sweeter your blood when I kill you!~ [TAZOK02]
@4468   = ~I will have your head!~ [TAZOK03]
@4469   = ~No begging's gonna help you now!~ [TAZOK04]
@4470   = ~Oh sure! Touch me like you know me! Now I kill you twice!~ [TAZOK05]
@4471   = ~Maybe you will stay quiet when you're dead!~ [TAZOK06]
@4472   = ~Do I LOOK like I enjoy being prodded by strangers? Stow the pointer, mouse-boy!~ [TAZOK07]
@4473   = ~So the stoic adventurers have found their way down to my lair.~ [DAVEO01]
@4474   = ~You meddling fools, your victory shall be short lived.~ [DAVEO02]
@4475   = ~Die, insolent whelps!~ [DAVEO03]
@4476   = ~Ah ha ha ha ha ha!~ [DAVEO04]
@4477   = ~Your efforts are futile!~ [DAVEO05]
@4478   = ~Tremble before the might of my sorcery!~ [DAVEO06]
@4479   = ~Your feeble skills are no match for my magic!~ [DAVEO07]
@4480   = ~You there! Identify yourselves!~ [ALDET01]
@4481   = ~Come now, old chaps, can't we be friends?~ [ALDET02]
@4482   = ~For Baldur's Gate!~ [ALDET03]
@4483   = ~Learn some manners, brute.~ [ALDET04]
@4484   = ~Nothing is more vulgar than bad manners.~ [ALDET05]
@4485   = ~Learn to bathe, lout.~ [ALDET06]
@4486   = ~Oh my goodness!~ [ALDET07]
@4487   = ~Greetings, taxpayers. I am Duke Eltan, commander of the Flaming Fist.~ [ELTAN01]
@4488   = ~Insolent madmen. Guards! To arms!~ [ELTAN03]
@4489   = ~By all that's holy!~ [ELTAN04]
@4490   = ~Honorable men are hard to come by.~ [ELTAN05]
@4491   = ~The common folk are the true rulers of this land.~ [ELTAN06]
@4492   = ~I AM the law.~ [ELTAN07]
@4493   = ~Citizens, please step forward.~ [SCARR01]
@4494   = ~If it's a fight you want, a fight I'll give you!~ [SCARR03]
@4495   = ~I am a man of my word.~ [SCARR04]
@4496   = ~Evil finds its worst enemy in truth and honor.~ [SCARR05]
@4497   = ~Oh my bum's itchy, but I can't scratch it 'cause my armor's too tight.~ [SCARR06]
@4498   = ~The Flaming Fist aren't mercenaries. They're this city's police force!~ [SCARR07]
@4499   = ~All I wish is to continue my journey! Friends await, while I must suffer this tiresome dance?! Does the mere mention of Drizzt attract your ilk?!~ [DRIZT01]
@4500   = ~ 'Tis your lives to waste!~ [DRIZT03]
@4501   = ~I am a gentle man at heart. At least, when I'm not slaughtering the stupid.~ [DRIZT04]
@4502   = ~I've sparred with demons from the Nine Hells themselves! I shall barely break a sweat here today!~ [DRIZT05]
@4503   = ~All this chatter is fine, but I've places I'd rather be.~ [DRIZT06]
@4504   = ~Don't poke Drizzt. 'Tis entirely unsociable.~ [DRIZT07]
@4505   = ~Ho there, wanderer. Stay thy course a moment to indulge an old man.~ [ELMIN01]
@4506   = ~Oh, it is most distressing that this is the course thou've chosen. I remove my support and will have no further dealings with thee.~ [ELMIN03]
@4507   = ~I can offer some guidance, but I will not interfere in your destiny.~ [ELMIN04]
@4508   = ~Thy mission is urgent! Must thou waste time poking the elderly?~ [ELMIN05]
@4509   = ~The years I have seen number hundreds, and yet I put up with thy prodding.~ [ELMIN06]
@4510   = ~Whoa, lord, it is hard to be humble when you're perfect in every way.~ [ELMIN07]
@4511   = ~Run as you will; you cannot hide forever!~ [SAREV02]
@4512   = ~Your death is inevitable.~ [SAREV03]
@4513   = ~Only the strongest shall prevail.~ [SAREV04]
@4514   = ~The streets will run red with blood when my work is finished.~ [SAREV05]
@4515   = ~Heh, I do not fear death... Do you?~ [SAREV06]
@4516   = ~Killing is our father's work; embrace it as I have.~ [SAREV07]
@4517   = ~You're perceptive for an old man. You know why I'm here. Hand over your ward and no one will be hurt. If you resist, it shall be a waste of your life.~ [SAREV10]
@4518   = ~I'm sorry that you feel that way, old man.~ [SAREV11]
@4519   = ~Ah, yes... the, ah... tab! Um... another ale, young miss. I'll be sure to have your funds ready.~ [VOLOO01]
@4520   = ~This is not my day at all!~ [VOLOO02]
@4521   = ~Perhaps some other time! I'm not in the mood for fighting today... or any day!~ [VOLOO03]
@4522   = ~ 'Tis surprising what one can learn at a simple country fair.~ [VOLOO04]
@4523   = ~I've traveled the length and breadth of Faerûn, and there's always something new.~ [VOLOO05]
@4524   = ~Awfully familiar with that pointer, aren't you? And after only one drink, too.~ [VOLOO06]
@4525   = ~I've a story for every man, woman, and child in Faerûn. However, copyright laws forbid me the telling.~ [VOLOO07]
@4526   = ~Salutations. I am Cadderly, a visitor of Candlekeep, like yourselves.~ [CADER01]
@4527   = ~Violence is never the wisest course.~ [CADER03]
@4528   = ~Faith is all one needs to surpass life's obstacles.~ [CADER04]
@4529   = ~You are a special one in the eyes of the gods.~ [CADER05]
@4530   = ~Never let greed or malice guide your destiny.~ [CADER06]
@4531   = ~One is not forced to walk in the steps of their father.~ [CADER07]
@4532   = ~Look it, Krystin, honey. It's the heroes of the Sword Coast. They're the real deal.~ [SLYTH01]
@4533   = ~It looks like tough times for us, honey.~ [SLYTH02]
@4534   = ~Hey, fellas, guess what time it is? Yep, you got it: it's time to die.~ [SLYTH03]
@4535   = ~Krystin, love, keep your mind on your work. We're professionals over here.~ [SLYTH04]
@4536   = ~Krystin, honey, don't break down on me here. I still need your help!~ [SLYTH05]
@4537   = ~Shut up and bleed faster.~ [SLYTH06]
@4538   = ~I once met a man from Nantucket... Oh, wrong world.~ [SLYTH07]
@4539   = ~Ohhh! I'm so excited, Slythe. I've never heard real live heroes beg for their lives.~ [KRYST01]
@4540   = ~I can't take this! I can't. I'm sorry, darling.~ [KRYST02]
@4541   = ~You're all going to die. I'm going to slit your throats, open up your guts, and spoon out your brains.~ [KRYST03]
@4542   = ~Blood makes me giddy. I love to see it in great big spurts.~ [KRYST04]
@4543   = ~Oh, ohhh, you bastards, you hurt me. They hurt me, honey. DIIIEEE, die, die, AAARGGHH.~ [KRYST05]
@4544   = ~Ninety nine buckets of blood on the wall, ninety nine buckets of blood.~ [KRYST06]
@4545   = ~He he he he.~ [KRYST07]
@4546   = ~None cross Greywolf and live!~ [GREYW01]
@4547   = ~You've not heard the last of this, ye worthless priggers!~ [GREYW02]
@4548   = ~Have at thee, ye thieving scoundrel!~ [GREYW03]
@4549   = ~No one meddles with my business lest they become it!~ [GREYW04]
@4550   = ~All o' you deserve the morning drop on the gallows.~ [GREYW05]
@4551   = ~Stupid cullys.~ [GREYW06]
@4552   = ~The back of my hand or the tip of my boot. Take your pick.~ [GREYW07]
@4553   = ~Wait! Me no want fight... Me Korax, me friend!~ [KORAX01]
@4554   = ~Me kill your enemies, yes me will!~ [KORAX03]
@4555   = ~Korax hungry, mmmmmm, very hungry.~ [KORAX04]
@4556   = ~Korax thinks you look very tasty today.~ [KORAX05]
@4557   = ~Korax good dog, yes, good dog!~ [KORAX06]
@4558   = ~Korax sorry, but he so very hungry. He must eat now! He must eat you!~ [KORAX07]
@4559   = ~Greetingshh, fellow rogues. *hic*~ [HUSAM01]
@4560   = ~There are too many. Retreat!~ [HUSAM02]
@4561   = ~The Shadow Thieves send their regards.~ [HUSAM03]
@4562   = ~*hic* I's thinks I hads too much to drinks.~ [HUSAM04]
@4563   = ~~ [HUSAM05]
@4564   = ~You know, one day... I'lls have me mys revengsh. Ha ha ha ha ha! *hic* *burp*~ [HUSAM06]
@4565   = ~Lying, causing terror, and murder—those are my pastimes.~ [HUSAM07]
@4566   = ~As all of you know, this is a special occasion for the city of Baldur's Gate.~ [LIIAJ01]
@4567   = ~The evidence we have about Entar's murder does resemble the work of the Shadow Thieves, but...~ [LIIAJ04]
@4568   = ~If I MAY continue, the signature left behind was very blatant and could have put there to mislead all of us.~ [LIIAJ05]
@4569   = ~Could we all have a round of applause for Silke Rosena? She is a performer who hails from Berdusk.~ [BELTT01]
@4570   = ~The votes have been tallied from those submitted by the landowners. The result was nearly unanimous.~ [BELTT04]
@4571   = ~All of your questions will be answered in due time; you need not worry.~ [BELTT05]
@4572   = ~Perhaps I could interject something before this meeting degenerates into meaningless bickering.~ [BELTT06]
@4573   = ~Wait one moment, that is not in your power to decide.~ [BELTT07]
@4574   = ~What of Duke Eltan, has his condition improved at all? If he dies, who will replace him?~ [PNOBL01]
@4575   = ~What about the rumors of Amn mobilizing for war? Why aren't we preparing for war?~ [PNOBL02]
@4576   = ~With our iron shortage, how are we to defend ourselves? And who will give us the iron we need?~ [PNOBL03]
@4577   = ~Entar was killed by Shadow Thieves, agents of Amn. If it isn't obvious to the rest of you, it's obvious to me: Amn wants a war.~ [PNOBL04]
@4578   = ~I believe that Eltan was poisoned by members of the Shadow Thieves. They're obviously trying to kill our leaders.~ [PNOBL05]
@4579   = ~Resembles?! That's ridiculous. The signature left behind on the body WAS the mark of the Shadow Thieves. Are you blind AND stupid, woman?!~ [PNOBL06]
@4580   = ~Who would want to mislead us?!~ [PNOBL07]
@4581   = ~What of the Zhentarim? I've heard that they may be somehow involved.~ [PNOBL08]
@4582   = ~Shut up, let Sarevok speak.~ [PNOBL09]
@4583   = ~Stop! You go nowhere! This our bridge. You pay to walk it!~ [GNARL01]
@4584   = ~Me Gnarl... Me hungry!~ [GNARL02]
@4585   = ~Yeah, you pay... 20 gold for each head, or lose head!~ [HAIRT01]
@4586   = ~Mmmm... smell good.~ [HAIRT02]
@4587   = ~Hey dere, I'm Caldo, and dis is my brother Krumm.~ [CALDO01]
@4588   = ~Me's gonna to be rich!~ [CALDO02]
@4589   = ~Uhhhh... yeah.~ [KRUMM01]
@4590   = ~No more for you.~
@4591   = ~Duhhhhhhh...~ [KRUMM02]
@4592   = ~Where's me ale, woman?~
@4593   = ~Please, kind spirits! A wondrous ancient oak is in peril...~ [DRYAA01]
@4594   = ~My tree is in such pain!~ [DRYAA02]
@4595   = ~Ahh, beauteous creature! You are my masterpiece!~ [PRISM01]
@4596   = ~Soon... my work will be done.~ [PRISM02]
@4597   = ~Someone disturbs me?!~ [ULRAN01]
@4598   = ~My station is much greater than that of Tethtoril's. Hmmmph!~ [ULRAN02]
@4599   = ~Greetings, young one.~ [TETHT01]
@4600   = ~I am very proud of you, as I am sure Gorion is.~ [TETHT02]
@4601   = ~In the Year of the Turrets, a great host will come from the east like a plague of locusts. So sayeth the wise Alaundo.~ [CHANT01]
