@6875   = ~A crossbow is a bow mounted crosswise on a wooden or metal shaft, the latter called a tiller. The bow is usually made of ash or yew. The crossbow fires a quarrel (also called a bolt). Light crossbows weigh less than their heavy counterparts and can be used by all kinds of rogues.

