@6879   = ~Aha! I understand it! Sorry to bother your petty concerns, but I have translated some of the Nether Scroll.~ [EDWIN84]
@6880   = ~Hmm... another revelation in my... er... our Nether Scroll. A spell of transformation, both basic and sophisticated. It is not unlike the transformation of mage to lich... but it must be more... much more...~ [EDWIN85]
@6881   = ~Light Crossbow~
@6882   = ~Dagger of Throwing +3: Firetooth~
@6883   = ~Light Crossbow~
@6884   = ~Light Crossbow +1~
@6885   = ~I've prepared for this moment all my life, and lifetimes before! Be prepared to cower and flee! Nothing will stand in my way after this!~
@6886   = ~Edwin, I'd suggest restraint. It's dangerous to meddle with magic that you know nothing about.~
@6887   = ~Go ahead, Edwin. A powerful mage is difficult to find, and of terrific benefit to all.~
@6888   = ~Light Crossbow of Speed +1: The Army Scythe~
@6889   = ~The cloak can be made in every possible shape with just about every type of fabric. The most common forms are a circular piece of fabric with a hole in the center for the head, and fabric draped from neck, connected by a chain, brooch, cord, or pins.

STATISTICS:

Weight: 3~
