@15196  = ~My name is <GABBER>. Who might you be?~
@15197  = ~I lost my spell. Sorry.~ [AERIE42]
@15198  = ~That's because I haven't been in the Copper Coronet for very long. That doesn't mean we can't be friends, though, does it?~
@15199  = ~~
@15200  = ~W-we w... we will continue this another day!~ [ANOMEN03]
@15201  = ~Verily, heh... I am pleased at the progress that this ill-conceived group has made. I had not thought such a thing possible.~ [ANOMEN04]
@15202  = ~And I don't recognize you. What of it?~
@15203  = ~Hmph! I am barely convinced that honor even holds a place of importance here. I shall see and judge for myself.~ [ANOMEN05]
@15204  = ~I'll not associate with one who smells like he slipped into a vat of spirits. Excuse me.~
@15205  = ~Truly, your actions lack virtue! Change your ways quickly or suffer my wrath!~ [ANOMEN06]
@15206  = ~Enough! I can take no more of this company! From here on, we are as enemies!~ [ANOMEN07]
@15207  = ~Now, you have obviously given considerable thought to the future of this group. I accept the charge—gladly!~ [ANOMEN08]
@15208  = ~Oy, my apologeesh, me <PRO_LADYLORD>. I'm told itsh been a hard day, and I shpose I'm glad I can't 'member a none o' it.~
@15209  = ~I demand that we stop. The day was not this long even when I led soldiers in the Order!~ [ANOMEN09]
@15210  = ~Well, I be Garoll, thank ye. *burp* (Who wash 'at?) Now that you an' I be proper frendsh an' all, how aboutsh you buyin Garoll a drink, aye?~
@15211  = ~Conjure Fire Elemental~
@15212  = ~Conjure Fire Elemental
(Conjuration/Summoning)

Level: 6
Sphere: Elemental (Fire), Summoning
Range: 25 ft.
Duration: 1 turn/level
Casting Time: 9
Area of Effect: Special
Saving Throw: None

Upon casting a Conjure Fire Elemental spell, the caster opens a special gate to the Elemental Plane of Fire, and a fire elemental is summoned in the vicinity of the caster. There is a 60% chance that a 12-Hit-Dice elemental appears; a 35% chance that a 16-Hit-Dice elemental appears; and a 5% chance that a 24-Hit-Dice elemental appears. The elemental will do the bidding of the caster until it is slain or the duration of the spell runs out. All the commands given to the elemental are done telepathically, so there is no time lost due to miscommunication and no need to know the language of the summoned creature. Unlike Mages, priests do not have to engage in a battle of the minds to control their elemental.~
@15213  = ~Why do we pace about when there is evil to be fought?! *sigh* There is no glory in watching the grass grow!~ [ANOMEN10]
@15214  = ~For the Order!~ [ANOMEN11]
@15215  = ~Righteousness shall prevail!~ [ANOMEN12]
@15216  = ~You shall suffer my wrath!~ [ANOMEN13]
@15217  = ~~ [ANOMEN14]
@15218  = ~~ [ANOMEN15]
@15219  = ~I need speedy assistance, my friend, or I shall not be able to fight on!~ [ANOMEN16]
@15220  = ~These trees and glades hide horrors of all manner... Watch your backs!~ [ANOMEN17]
@15221  = ~High Merchant Logan Coprith~
@15222  = ~Pfeh! A dank pool of base corruption if ever there was one. Why, if not for the Order, the gods would surely smite man for such sins.~ [ANOMEN18]
@15223  = ~High Merchant Logan Coprith~
@15224  = ~Aye, 'tis good to adventure in such a place! The blood quickens knowing that evil is so near!~ [ANOMEN19]
