@17650  = ~Kolssed~
@17651  = ~Kolssed~
@17652  = ~When activated, the wand will eject a missile of magical energy that darts forth and unerringly strikes its target. This includes enemy creatures in a melee. The target creature must be seen or otherwise detected to be hit, however, so near-total concealment, such as that offered by arrow slits, can render the spell ineffective. The missile will inflict 1d4+1 points of damage.

STATISTICS:

Charge abilities:
– 1 magic missile will strike the target
  Damage: 1d4+1
  Range: 25 ft.
  Area of Effect: 1 creature

Requires:
 9 Intelligence

Weight: 1

Not usable by:
 Wizard Slayer~
@17653  = ~When used, this wand shoots forth a thin ray of bluish color to a maximum range of 25 ft. When a creature is touched by the ray, it must save vs. wand in order to avoid being stunned for 1 turn.

STATISTICS:

Charge abilities:
– Stun target (save vs. wand at -4 penalty negates)
  Range: 25 ft.
  Area of Effect: 1 creature
  Duration: 1 turn

Requires:
 9 Intelligence

Weight: 1

Not usable by:
 Barbarian
 Cleric
 Fighter
 Druid
 Ranger
 Monk
 Paladin
 Thief~
@17654  = ~The wand will cough forth a huge, burning ball of fire that streaks out to the desired range (to a maximum of 25 ft.) and bursts in a fiery, violent blast, just like the Fireball spell. The fireball inflicts 6d6 points of damage, but all 1s rolled are counted as 2s. The victim(s) may make a save vs. wand in order to take only half damage. The second ability of the wand is akin to the spell Agannazar's Scorcher in that a column of flame will streak towards the victim inflicting 6d6+6 damage, with a save vs. wand for half.

STATISTICS:

Charge abilities:
– Fireball
  Damage: 6d6 fire damage (save vs. wand for half)
  Range: 25 ft.
  Area of Effect: 15-ft. radius

– Agannazar's Scorcher
  Damage: 6d6+6 fire damage (save vs. wand for half)
  Range: 25 ft.
  Area of Effect: 2-ft. by 40-ft. jet

Requires:
 9 Intelligence

Weight: 1

Not usable by:
