 Sorcerer~
@66204  = ~I was to give birth to one of the Children. To you. I rose my arms up and hailed my Lord of Murder with great joy at my fate.~ [D1MOTH08]
@66205  = ~Others of Bhaal's order took me away, to hide us in the darkest temple, away from prying eyes. Others of the Children were there... and when our great Bhaal died did we begin our task.~ [D1MOTH09]
@66206  = ~Her task was to slay her own child, sacrifice her babe upon the bloodiest of altars.~ [D1GORI01]
@66207  = ~I would slay you, my child. So Bhaal could live again.~ [D1MOTH10]
@66208  = ~But I and several of my colleagues had discovered the location of this temple. We attacked and stopped your mother from performing the sacrifice.~ [D1GORI02]
@66209  = ~We resisted. This was the will of Bhaal, father of my child.~ [D1MOTH11]
@66210  = ~They were many, and their magic was strong. We had little time. I killed the priestess...~ [D1GORI03]
@66211  = ~He slew me, your mother!~ [D1MOTH12]
@66212  = ~I rescued you and fled from the temple even as many other Bhaalspawn babes died.~ [D1GORI04]
@66213  = ~But not all of us died. Some of us used the chaos to escape, to flee.~ [D1SARE01]
@66214  = ~Yes. Not all the Bhaalspawn children died that night. I saved the only one I could.~ [D1GORI05]
@66215  = ~He could only save one; there was no time for more. But I was there as well.~ [D1SARE02]
@66216  = ~I chose you. I could not save both of you.~ [D1GORI06]
@66217  = ~He left ME behind, saving you instead.~ [D1SARE03]
@66218  = ~It could have been either of you. There was only time to choose one.~
@66219  = ~And so I fled on my own, raised by foster parents in the Iron Throne.~ [D1SARE04]
@66220  = ~It was a choice made in a second. It haunted me forever, for I never knew what became of the child.~
@66221  = ~It mattered not. I killed Gorion in the end.~ [D1SARE05]
@66222  = ~Yes, the child alone knew of the Bhaalspawn I hid. The child was Sarevok.~
@66223  = ~Eye of Tyr~
